{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted draft/submission.json (action=explore) with draft/explore-harness-lease.go: an exploration to sharpen the last substantive lead on the frontier rather than a fixed check, because the construction runs did not isolate the behaviour well enough to submit as evidence. The lead is whether a leader's own lease check can depose it while a quorum of voters is reachable, given that the leader's contact refresh interval is derived from HeartbeatTimeout while LeaderLeaseTimeout is fixed at creation. The harness connects three in-memory voters, waits for one to be elected, lengthens that leader's own intervals through the public ReloadConfig to a 300 second heartbeat and election timeout while the lease stays at five seconds, waits twelve seconds, and then records the leader's state and term, its peers' states and terms, and whether a peer still answers a probe in the leader's term. Its output is retained as construction knowledge and is honestly ambiguous: the leader ended as a Follower while one peer had been elected Leader in a later term and the third voter answered the probe, which is consistent with the lease deposing the leader but equally consistent with the peer's higher term, because the peers kept the short timeouts they were created with and campaigned inside the window. The rationale therefore names the discriminator that would settle it — an observation of the leader's own state transition and the term it held at that moment, before any peer's higher term arrives, together with the peers' reachability at that instant — and records why the reload path matters: ReloadConfig accepts the change, validating only that the lease does not exceed the heartbeat timeout, so the library can itself move a running node from a coherent lease relation into an incoherent one. No target file was modified and no property was claimed; this product creates no Evidence and no map version, so the lead remains open on the lease behaviour while the run's confirmed results stand at six in-scope findings plus one reviewed bounded negative. Optional preflight with the trusted validator returned valid=true.\"}"}}
